---
const brewCommands = "brew tap ChristianVilen/ku-ka\nbrew install --cask kuka";
const quarantineCommand = "sudo xattr -d com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Ku-Ka.app";
---
<section id="install" class="dark-band bg-graphite px-6 py-28 text-graphite-ink">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(1.85rem,3vw+0.5rem,2.75rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em]">
      Install.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-[10px] border border-graphite-rule bg-graphite-2">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-graphite-rule px-4 py-2.5">
        <span class="mono-label !text-graphite-muted">Homebrew</span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-copy" data-copy={brewCommands}>Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed"><code><span class="text-accent-bright">$</span> brew tap ChristianVilen/ku-ka
<span class="text-accent-bright">$</span> brew install --cask kuka</code></pre>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-12 font-display text-xl font-medium">First launch: get past Gatekeeper.</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[60ch] text-graphite-muted">
      Ku-Ka is unsigned, so macOS blocks it once. Clear the quarantine flag
      and it opens normally from then on:
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 rounded-[10px] border border-graphite-rule bg-graphite-2">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-graphite-rule px-4 py-2.5">
        <span class="mono-label !text-graphite-muted">Terminal</span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-copy" data-copy={quarantineCommand}>Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed"><code><span class="text-accent-bright">$</span> sudo xattr -d com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Ku-Ka.app</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[60ch] text-sm text-graphite-muted">
      Prefer the GUI? Try opening Ku-Ka once, then
      <strong class="font-medium text-graphite-ink">System Settings → Privacy&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Security → "Open Anyway"</strong>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-12 font-display text-xl font-medium">Then grant two permissions.</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[60ch] text-graphite-muted">
      <strong class="font-medium text-graphite-ink">Accessibility</strong> powers the
      shortcuts and window tiling; <strong class="font-medium text-graphite-ink">Screen
      Recording</strong> powers the capture itself. macOS asks for both on first
      use. If either gets stuck, the troubleshooting section below covers it.
    </p>

    <p class="mono-label mt-14 !text-graphite-muted">
      macOS 14 (Sonoma) or later · <a href="https://github.com/ChristianVilen/ku-ka/releases/latest" class="underline decoration-graphite-rule underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-graphite-ink hover:decoration-accent-bright">.zip on GitHub Releases</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
